spans.s:
√piś (piṃśáti, -te [758]; pipéśa, pipiśé;
piṣṭá). adorn. [cf. ποικίλος, AS. fāh,
‘many-colored’; Lat. pic-tor, ‘painter.’]

√piṣ (pináṣṭi; pipéṣa, pipiṣé; ápiṣat;
pekṣyáti; piṣṭá; péṣṭum; piṣṭvā́; -píṣya
). crush; grind, 47^5; mill. [cf. Lat.
pinsere, pīsere, ‘crush’: of doubtful kinship
is πτίσσω, ‘pound, husk.’]
+ sam, crush together or to pieces.
